phase 3
Prompt A: Create an artwork that mimics a sculpture-like drawing and tells a story about the hierarchy and political power of the Mesopotamian era. Use only primary colors and simple figures to emphasize how storytelling/communication were conveyed through drawings. Add rough textures and harsh lines to insinuate a difference between social classes as well. Adjust the artwork as needed to present a historical feel to the overall piece. 
Theme A: Art as political power and stability
Prompt B: Create a manuscript illumination from the medieval period that shows dedication to the evangelical basis of Christianity. There should be lots of color and a carpet-like texture to the piece, but it should not disturb the overall balance. Add emphasis on the geometrical shapes and hard line breaks as details in the artwork. The artwork should clearly contextualize the spiritual importance. 
Theme B: Art as devotional labor and sacred text
